The look of modama's design (mgmtinterface-new/DESIGN.md)

Upstream's own colours and font never apply: tailwind.config.ts defines the eosc-*
colours and Roboto, but Tailwind v4 reads that file only through @config, which
index.css does not have (RepositoryStats.tsx says so: "Tailwind eosc-* tokens are
no-ops under v4"). The page's colours come from hex values in its class names and
from Tailwind's default palette. Put modama's design in the theme Tailwind v4 reads,
so that the colours are set in one place:

- index.css: an @theme block. DESIGN.md's colours are Tailwind v3's blue and slate
  scales: the blue-* classes get v3's blues (v4's differ), the gray-* classes the
  slate scale, upstream's eosc-* names DESIGN.md's tokens (a comment names each).
  Plus Jakarta Sans and JetBrains Mono instead of Roboto, from Google Fonts as in
  mgmtinterface-new; font-light at 400, DESIGN.md's lightest weight.
- The hex values in class names become the eosc-* names (the sed command below);
  the results page's gradient becomes the background colour.
- RepositoryStats.tsx: the chart colours, which take values, not classes, get the
  same values.

To make it again on a new upstream version, in its source:

  grep -rlE '\-\[#(002337|646363|009FE3|1A1A1A|E0E0E0|FAFAFA|3b7dd8|E5E7EB)\]' src --include=*.tsx \
    | xargs sed -i -E 's/-\[#002337\]/-eosc-dark-blue/g; s/-\[#646363\]/-eosc-gray/g;
        s/-\[#009FE3\]/-eosc-light-blue/g; s/-\[#1A1A1A\]/-eosc-text/g;
        s/-\[#E0E0E0\]/-eosc-border/g; s/-\[#FAFAFA\]/-eosc-bg/g;
        s/-\[#3b7dd8\]/-blue-500/g; s/-\[#E5E7EB\]/-gray-200/g'

then the edits to index.css, RepositoryStats.tsx and SearchPage.tsx as here. Only the
look changes; upstream could take it as a theme, and this patch would go.

Applies to matchmaker v0.14.0 (e7138c898926ebb79e45dd7d20cbf838dcf5dbe5) after 0001 to 0003.

